Subject: marc_post: the boot-class modules after root is mounted

dlm_marc_post(), which the kernel calls once after vfs_mountroot returns,
reads the manifest the loader booted (amix-dlm
docs/contracts/C3-5-module-member.md): it registers every demand-class
record's character majors= for that module, so the first open loads it,
then loads every boot-class record in manifest order, unless its match=
keys name no board here (the platform's dlm_plat_match; "always" always
matches).  Each outcome is one console line.  In safe mode (dlm_safe,
the platform's, from the loader record) nothing loads, and every other
load -- a first open, modload -- is refused (30 section 3).  Every load of a
manifest member passes the member's param records to its _load as one
string "<pname>=<value> ...", valid during the call.
30-module-core.md section 3, section 2 patch 16 (the boot-class half;
marc_root comes with the arena load path).

